.intro-shade{position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:10;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:18px;background:#09110deF;touch-action:auto}
---
.intro-card{width:min(560px,96%);padding:clamp(20px,4vw,36px);border:1px solid #9db17c;border-radius:20px;background:#24352b;box-shadow:0 18px 60px #0008;text-align:center}
---
<p>Move with <strong>WASD</strong>, the arrow keys, or the on-screen controls. Press <strong>E</strong> near a station to interact.</p>

Fix CSS:
```
.intro-shade{...align-items:flex-start;overflow:auto;...}
.intro-card{margin:auto;...}
```
And add media short height:
```
@media(max-height:560px){.intro-card{padding:16px}.intro-card h1{font-size:26px;margin-bottom:8px}.intro-card p{margin:6px auto;line-height:1.45;font-size:13px}.intro-card .objective{padding:9px}.intro-card button{margin-top:8px;padding:10px 22px}}
```
This makes it fit more likely to fit in 390 height? Let's estimate: padding 32, h1 26*1.1=29 + margin 8, p1 maybe 2 lines 38, objective maybe 7 lines at 13*1.45=19 → 133, last p 2 lines 38, button 44, margins 18 → 32+37+44+133+38+44+18 = 346 < 390. Could actually fit! Great. But at 390 height with padding 18*2=36, available 354; card 346 fits. Good, maybe no scroll needed. At 320 height, scroll works.

Update CSS. Also `touch-action:auto` on shade; overflow auto on touch should scroll. Add `-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch`? Not necessary.

Let's edit.

Add media query to short heights. We can append after the existing media queries in the final style block. The relevant end:
```
@media(max-width:700px) and (orientation:portrait){...}
</style>
